      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 11B</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>A COPY OF FORM 990 IS REVIEWED BY THE HEAD OF FINANCE AND ACCOUNTING AND THE CEO. THE ORGANIZATION IS IN THE PROCESS OF CHANGING ITS BOARD, THEREFORE, A COPY OF THE 990 IS PROVIDED TO BOARD MEMBERS AFTER SUBMISSION TO THE IRS.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 12C</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>A CONTRACT OR TRANSACTION IN WHICH A DIRECTOR OR OFFICER HAS FINANCIAL INTEREST, SHALL ONLY BE AUTHORIZED BY THE BOARD OF THE DIRECTORS OR THE COMMITTEE THEREOF UNDER THE FOLLOWING CONDITIONS: A) THE MATERIAL FACTS OF THE RELATIONSHIP OR INTEREST AS TO THE CONTRACT OR TRANSACTION ARE FULLY DISCLOSED TO THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS OR COMMITTEE WHO AUTHORIZES THE CONTRACT OR TRANSACTION BY THE AFFIRMATIVE VOTE OF A MAJORITY OF THE DISINTERESTED DIRECTORS AND OFFICERS B) THE CONTRACT OR TRANSACTION IS FAIR AS TO THE CORPORATION AS OF THE TIME IT IS AUTHORIZED, APPROVED OR RATIFIED BY THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS. AT A MEETING OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS IN WHICH THE AUTHORIZATION OF A CONTRACT OR TRANSACTION IS IN QUESTION, THE COMMON OR INTERESTED DIRECTORS MAY BE COUNTED IN DETERMINING THE PRESCENCE OF A QUORUM.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 15</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>APPROVED COMPENSATION PACKAGE FOR CEO IS OUTLINED IN CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY, INCLUDES BOARD APPROVAL, DIRECTOR RESCUSAL, IF APPLICABLE, COMPARABILITY DATE, AND IN SOME CASES A THIRD-PARTY COMPENSATION STUDY.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION C, LINE 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>THE ORGANIZATION MAKES ITS GOVERNING DOCUMENTS AND CONFLICT OF INTEREST POLICY AVAILABLE TO THE PUBLIC UPON REQUEST.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>OTHER INFORMATION</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>CONSTELLATION RESEARCH CENTER INC. (CRC) WAS FOUNDED BY REDWOOD RESEARCH GROUP, INC. (REDWOOD) A 501(C)(3) ORGANIZATION DURING 2023. CRC WAS FORMED TO TAKE OVER REDWOOD'S CONSTELLATION PROGRAM WHICH PROVIDES CO-WORKING SPACES, EQUIPMENT AND RELATED RESOURCES TO FACILITATE COLLABORATIVE RESEARCH AMONG MISSION-ALIGNED ENTITIES. THE CONSTELLATION PROGRAM WAS GRANTED TO CRC IN 2023. THE RESTRUCTURE OVERALL ALLOWS BOTH ORGANIZATIONS TO INCREASE CAPACITIES TO CARRY OUT THEIR RESPECTIVE ACTIVITIES AND MORE EFFECTIVELY PURSUE THEIR SHARED MISSION. DUE TO THE COMPLEXITIES OF GRANTING THE CONSTELLATION PROGRAM, CRC IS IN THE PROCESS OF COMPLETING ITS GAAP AUDIT OF THE FINANCIAL STATEMENTS. UPON COMPLETION OF THE GAAP AUDIT, CRC WILL BE FILING AN AMENDED FORM 990. ALL INFORMATION CONTAINED IN THIS SUBMISSION WAS BASED ON THE BEST INFORMATION AVAILABLE AT THE TIME OF FILING.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
